{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386322-black-spiral-dancers-before-the-fall-of-white-howlers","id":1386322,"title":"Black Spiral Dancers before the fall of White Howlers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-07T01:50:27-07:00","id":1386322,"title":"Black Spiral Dancers before the fall of White Howlers?","content":"So we all know BSDs come from WHs. But why didn\u2019t they exist before the fall of WHs?<br /> <br /> I mean, wyrmish garou which devote themselves to Wyrm should exist all the time. But it seems that Garou Nation didn\u2019t know anything about this until BSDs rose, doesn\u2019t it strange?<br /> <br /> Or wyrmish garou do exist at the beginning, but too small to form a Tribe and be noticed by most garou?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 05-07-2020, 08:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T01:58:41-07:00","id":1386325,"title":"","content":"Some interesting stuff:<br /> The 1000 Hells, Page 116<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hengeyokai who willingly subject themselves to the Yama Kings are rare. <b>Most instead choose to walk the Ebon Maze and enter the direct device of the Centipede(aka. Wyrm), a vast force of elemental evil that lays beneath (and may say stands behind) the lords of Yomi Wan. </b> </div> </div> </div>So, if wyrmish garou can be considered as BSD, I think they should exist all the time<br /> <br /> It is odd that most garou don\u2019t know it until BSD appeared...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:06:40-07:00","id":1386327,"title":"","content":"There is some examples: The First Metis of the Red Talons, The Number Two of the Shadow Lords. The diferences is the Black Spiral Dancrs are an entire tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2250-magus","name":"Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:07:27-07:00","id":1386329,"title":"","content":"I think there is a difference between a Garou who has fallen to the Wyrm, and a tribe of such Garou with an Incarna totem as patron.<br /> <br /> There is probably some important elements of the history of the Black Spiral Dancers missing from the sourcebooks which would explain how they won the patronage of Whippoorwill.<br /> <br /> I think there's several distinct elements to the story of the BSDs. These typically get put together, but they're not actually the same thing. There's the corruption of many members of the White Howlers. The destruction of the uncorrupted members. The walking of the Black Spiral as the specific means of corruption. And the winning of Whippoorwill as the totem.<br /> <br /> Before the creation of the tribe, there could be individual members of the Garou who fell to the Wyrm. But they lacked the numbers and influence to form a tribe, so there wasn't one. There was simply lone Garou or low numbers of Garou in a pack who might at best earn a pack totem. They didn't have a tribal patron. But after the mass corruption of the White Howlers and their becoming a tribe, any time a Garou fell to the Wyrm, they could go to the BSDs and join the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:09:07-07:00","id":1386330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386322-black-spiral-dancers-before-the-fall-of-white-howlers?p=1386327#post1386327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is some examples: The First Metis of the Red Talons, The Number Two of the Shadow Lords. The diferences is the Black Spiral Dancrs are an entire tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but Dark Age Werewolf say most garou still think only WH can walk the spiral, and BSDs used this to spread themselves quite quickly<br /> <br /> I wonder why they didn\u2019t know all garou are corruptable","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:11:52-07:00","id":1386332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386322-black-spiral-dancers-before-the-fall-of-white-howlers?p=1386329#post1386329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a difference between a Garou who has fallen to the Wyrm, and a tribe of such Garou with an Incarna totem as patron.<br /> <br /> There is probably some important elements of the history of the Black Spiral Dancers missing from the sourcebooks which would explain how they won the patronage of Whippoorwill.<br /> <br /> I think there's several distinct elements to the story of the BSDs. These typically get put together, but they're not actually the same thing. There's the corruption of many members of the White Howlers. The destruction of the uncorrupted members. The walking of the Black Spiral as the specific means of corruption. And the winning of Whippoorwill as the totem.<br /> <br /> Before the creation of the tribe, there could be individual members of the Garou who fell to the Wyrm. But they lacked the numbers and influence to form a tribe, so there wasn't one. There was simply lone Garou or low numbers of Garou in a pack who might at best earn a pack totem. They didn't have a tribal patron. But after the mass corruption of the White Howlers and their becoming a tribe, any time a Garou fell to the Wyrm, they could go to the BSDs and join the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Suit my second thought:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or wyrmish garou do exist at the beginning, but too small to form a Tribe and be noticed by most garou? </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:54:06-07:00","id":1386353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386322-black-spiral-dancers-before-the-fall-of-white-howlers#post1386322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or wyrmish garou do exist at the beginning, but too small to form a Tribe and be noticed by most garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the correct answer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:16:56-07:00","id":1386362,"title":"","content":"Yeah the thing is they pretty much always existed, even in Pangaea, but they didn't Unionize till a whole tribe fell. Before it was single individuals or packs that would fall, and that isn't enough manpower to develop rituals and lobby for Infernal clout. But when a whole Tribe Falls then they can interview for a Patron (Whippoorwill) and they can have an Embassy in Hell. So before the Whitehowlers fell you just have individual Anti-Saints like the First Ronin who didn't really have a legacy beyond his immortal self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:38:49-07:00","id":1386366,"title":"","content":"Up until the BSDs become a thing, I think the number of fully corrupted Garou (and Fera in general) is pretty low through most of history -- so low that each instance is a big deal. Up until the Howlers fall, I suspect the Fera believed that something on that scale was simply impossible. Corrupted Fera were rare and important, something that occurred maybe once a generation in a given region, and probably even less than that. Fully corrupted Garou and Fera could be dealt with - they were dangerous and significant, but manageable at significant cost.<br /> <br /> ...and then the BSD come along and everything changes. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Weaponized Ink: </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#141414\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/288291/Werewolf-The-Savage-Age-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: The Savage Age!</a> </span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11548-coyoteintx","name":"Coyoteintx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11548_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:44:28-07:00","id":1386371,"title":"","content":"Note that the Wars of Rage pretty much revolved around each Changing Breed assuming others were degenerates Fallen to the Wyrm, like the genociding of the Mokole because they were reptilian like the classical Wyrm visage of Dragons.<br /> <br /> And Kumo, the Goblin Spiders, were a Tribe of Wyrm worshippers that were quite populace before the BSDs.<br /> <br /> It was mostly that secret Fallen Shape Shifters were big deals, but the ones who couldn't keep it secret were tragedies rather then catastrophes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T06:19:02-07:00","id":1386377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Coyoteintx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386322-black-spiral-dancers-before-the-fall-of-white-howlers?p=1386366#post1386366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Up until the BSDs become a thing, I think the number of fully corrupted Garou (and Fera in general) is pretty low through most of history -- so low that each instance is a big deal. Up until the Howlers fall, I suspect the Fera believed that something on that scale was simply impossible. Corrupted Fera were rare and important, something that occurred maybe once a generation in a given region, and probably even less than that. Fully corrupted Garou and Fera could be dealt with - they were dangerous and significant, but manageable at significant cost.<br /> <br /> ...and then the BSD come along and everything changes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think fallen Fera are still rare in general up to now, although BSDs may make one or two more of each splats. After all they are few in total<br /> <br /> And Wyrm rose in the just last hundreds of years, at most. Especially after the Industrial Revolution, the deterioration speeded up a lot. Even in Dark Age werewolf still had the upper hand<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T09:58:43-07:00","id":1386424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1386322-black-spiral-dancers-before-the-fall-of-white-howlers?p=1386329#post1386329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there's several distinct elements to the story of the BSDs. These typically get put together, but they're not actually the same thing. There's the corruption of many members of the White Howlers. The destruction of the uncorrupted members. The walking of the Black Spiral as the specific means of corruption. And the winning of Whippoorwill as the totem.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends which story, I think. Walking the Black Spiral and winning Whippoorwill always happen, but the fall can go as you describe, corruption/destruction (as in Chronicles of the Black Labyrinth), or it can be one singular event, the tribe diving into Malfeas to face the Wyrm (the Tribebook).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T15:34:41-07:00","id":1386513,"title":"","content":"I largely agree with many of those who arrived to the question sooner then I that there have likely been Wyrm-tainted garou for nearly as long as the Wyrm has been fallen but that they were few and largely loose and scattered with enough to even create a pack being lucky.<br /> <br /> The fall of the White Howlers is important because it was the fall of an entire tribe to the Wyrm and thus a spiritual shifting of possession from Gaia to the Wyrm and creating the first large scale gathering of wyrm-tainted garou with enough spiritual resources to qualify as a tribe and gain recognition from a patron totem and the spirit courts as well as the Gaian tribes.<br /> <br /> There is also the definite factor that while the Wyrm has been considered a threat for millennia, its only been a threat on the scale that we know today since the Industrial Revolution or so. Sure it still had its bad days before the 1600s but everything escalated as time went on and yesterday's horrific tragedy became today's unpleasant fact-of-life. <br /> <br /> Add in the fact that Sense Wyrm is not the most discerning of gifts in that its somewhat binary in its readings, the xenophobic and clannish temperaments of many changing breeds, and religious hysteria over the relatively recent fall from paradise because of the Wyrm... well, when all you have is a hammer. The garou and other changing breeds followed their nature and this led to tragedies like the Wars of Rage and Impergium.<br /> <br /> As far as someone's earlier question about why the garou might think that their tribes wouldn't fall... probably pride. Garou are proud by nature and culturally they trend towards zealotry, superiority, and xenophobia. Garou are absolutely confident that they are Gaia's blessed champions and the favored children of their tribal totem - how could such paragons of virtue fall to the Wyrm? What happened to the White Howlers was a tragedy... yet surely their must have been some spiritual defect in Lion's Children for such a thing to even be possible, right?<br /> <br /> We see the same thing to this day with attitudes of victim-blaming and &quot;It can't happen here&quot; or those who see fires on the news but never expect it to happen to them.<br /> <br /> People simply aren't always rational and the garou and changing breeds are people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-11T10:25:56-07:00","id":1387538,"title":"","content":"I think their wered Balehound like Wyrm cults before the BSD's as such existed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}